  "goodToKnow": "Das Grundeinkommen is a basic income; das bedingungslose Grundeinkommen (BGE) is an unconditional basic income paid to everyone. It's widely debated in Germany. The association Mein Grundeinkommen ran a well-known study from 2021 to 2024 in which 122 people received €1,200 a month for three years; recipients mostly kept working. Germany's existing Bürgergeld is means-tested, so not unconditional. Plural: die Grundeinkommen."
